diff --git a/docs/DESIGN.md b/docs/DESIGN.md
index e5ce4086e49e8055cdcc0f0cb47b29b7bb68dd9e..4a51eb2a081e1d3606a4d5a8504fa68f3b94e3ad 100644
--- a/docs/DESIGN.md
+++ b/docs/DESIGN.md
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ repeat it. The header bar carries one primary control, one pencil, and one menu:
 
 - The primary control is Install, Start, or Stop, and it follows the state of the machine.
 - The pencil opens Machine Settings.
-- The menu carries Logs, Provision the Machine, Restart, and Delete Machine.
+- The menu carries Logs, Reprovision the Guest Agent, Restart, and Delete Machine.
 - Logs opens the log of the machine in the text editor: the console of the installer when it keeps one, else the service log of the machine.
 - The Serial Console and Remote Desktop dialogs state the user and the password with a copy control for each, because the guest asks for both at its login.
 - The Terminal and Remote Desktop dialogs carry Unlock the SSH Agent, which loads the key of the user into the dedicated agent of Phial and asks for the passphrase through pinentry.
@@ -90,10 +90,14 @@ - The install provisions the machine: it boots the guest once, waits for the guest agent to answer, copies the units of the guest into it, and stops it again.
 - The guest agent is the binary of Phial itself, so the reprovision step, which runs the provisioning again, replaces the agent of a machine as well.
 - The provisioning of a machine is idempotent, so the reprovision item in the menu of a machine runs it at any time.
 - The provisioning travels over the channel of the QEMU guest agent, which is a virtio serial port. The vsock carries the shell of the guest instead.
+- The QEMU guest agent of the guest runs in a confined SELinux domain, so the provisioning sends the script and the binary to /run/phial through the file API of the agent, and a path unit of the guest starts the service that runs the script as root without confinement.
+- The provisioning writes its own service and path units, so a machine that an older installer set up converges on the same state as a new install.
+- The page compares the build time of the host with the build time that the provisioning wrote into the guest, and asks for a reprovision with a banner when the guest is behind. The check reads /etc over the guest agent, because the confined domain reads nothing of the home of the user.
 - The guest turns plymouth off and masks the network wait, because a machine that waits for a splash or for the network never reaches a login.
 - The installer writes the home directory of the guest as root, so the provisioning repairs the labels of that directory before the session of the user writes its units.
 - A machine installs in minutes rather than seconds, so the first start of a fresh machine needs a few minutes before the guest answers.
-- The engine states the DRM native context of the host renderer, because a renderer without support for it leaves the guest without a working display.
+- The renderer of the host fails the DRM native context of Venus only when the guest initializes the GPU, so no probe can state it. A machine with such a renderer restarts once without the option and keeps that choice in its definition.
+- The stop of a machine asks the guest to shut down through the guest agent and presses the power button when no agent answers, so a stop flushes the writes of the guest; a guest that ignores the shutdown is switched off after a timeout.
 - The generated ssh configuration names no agent, so ssh uses the agent of the session, which asks for the passphrase of the key on the first use.
 
 Rules that the page keeps:
